  "_comment": [
    "Hand-written judgement for the glossary. scripts/extract_glossary.py reads",
    "this and never writes it, so re-extracting the notes can never destroy the",
    "decisions recorded here. Same split as tags.json against taxonomy.json in",
    "past-paper-questions-data/: the machine owns what it can read, this file",
    "owns what someone had to decide.",
    "",
    "THIS FILE MUST NOT CONTAIN A DEFINITION. Definitions come from the notes,",
    "verbatim, and nowhere else. Everything here is about which chip is a term",
    "and what to call it - never about what it means. If a definition is wrong,",
    "fix the notes page and re-extract.",
    "",
    "stopTerms   chip labels that are rhetorical section headings, not terms",
    "aliases     variant wording -> the canonical key it merges into",
    "display     canonical key -> the wording to show, when sources disagree",
    "tables      approved concept-table harvests, filled in at step 2.3",
    "formulaExclude  formula ids that are worked arithmetic, not formulae",
    "formulaLabel    formula id -> the name to show instead of its heading",
    "formulaTerms    formula id -> the term id it belongs to",
    "excludeSources   key -> notesUrls whose chip is not a definition of it",
    "preferredSources key -> notesUrls whose wording is canonical, best first",
    "",
    "BLOCKED, not rejected: f-economic-growth-indicators (Real GDP Growth) and",
    "f-interpreting-index-numbers-2 (Percentage Change) are excluded only because",
    "their LaTeX writes % unescaped, which TeX reads as a comment. See G3 in",
    "REVIEW-NOTES.md. Change % to \\% on the two notes pages and remove these two",
    "ids from formulaExclude and they render."
  ],
